2) SHARED REPRODUCIBILITY REQUIREMENTS (NEURIPS-STYLE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
R1. Locked data protocol:
  • Dataset: BNCI2014_001 motor imagery
  • Evaluation mode: cross-session (as currently stated)
  • Splits and preprocessing must be identical across all models/topologies.
  • If a split is currently generated by code:
      If split is deterministic given a seed, fix that seed and log it.
      Otherwise, pre-generate split indices once and reuse for all runs (recommended).

R2. Locked training protocol:
  • Optimizer: Adam
  • Max epochs: 200
  • Early stopping: patience 20
  • All hyperparameters fixed across models/topologies (unless explicitly specified as a conditional).
  • S seeds per topology (recommend S = 5, consistent with current draft).
  • Log: seed, topology ID, generator params, proxy values, runtime, best epoch, final metrics.

R3. Locked robustness protocol:
  • Same perturbation grid for all models.
  • Same evaluation metrics computed on the same test set.
  • If robustness evaluation has stochasticity (e.g., drift noise draws), fix a perturbation RNG seed per (topology, model seed, intensity)
    so curves are comparable and repeatable.

R4. Capacity controls:
  • Main plots should hold H fixed (strongly recommended) to avoid confounding.
  • Random sparse CfC baseline must be sparsity-matched:
      Option A (preferred): match E_active per selected topology.
      Option B: match average E_active across selected set (less strict; only if code cannot easily match per-topology).
  • Report parameter counts and E_active in Appendix.

R5. Reporting:
  • Use mean + 95% CI (bootstrap) for plots with curves.
  • State exactly what the CI is over:
      Prefer bootstrap over all (topology, seed) units (or over seeds nested in topology).

