4) EXPERIMENT 1 (PLOT 1): PROXY LANDSCAPE + COST ADVANTAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Motivation:
  Establish that proxy evaluation is cheap and yields a broad structural landscape; this justifies the two-stage method.

Core question:
  Does WS-Flex produce a diverse proxy distribution in ( \hat{TE}, \widehat{|ORC|} ) under a fixed proxy budget,
  and is proxy evaluation orders of magnitude cheaper than training + robustness sweeps?

Inputs:
  • Fixed H (main) + allowed generator params within bounds.
  • N_proxy connected graphs.

Procedure:
  E1.1 Proxy sampling loop:
    For trial i in 1..(until N_proxy connected graphs collected):
      - Deterministically set s_g (e.g., i or trial.number).
      - Sample θ within bounds (sampler can be TPE or uniform; log which).
      - Generate G_u = G(θ).
      - If disconnected: reject; increment reject counter; resample (do not update sampler if that is first-pass behavior).
      - Compute \hat{TE}(G_u), \widehat{|ORC|}(G_u).
      - Store record: θ, proxies, graph stats (|E|, E_active), runtime.

  E1.2 Proxy Pareto + selection overlay:
      - Compute Pareto set P in proxy space using f(G).
      - Select K graphs for training using diversity selection:
          Option A (preferred, simple): bin proxy space into a BxB grid (e.g., B=6) and sample from occupied Pareto bins.
          Option B: k-medoids / k-centers clustering in proxy plane on Pareto set, choose K cluster centers.

  E1.3 Cost accounting:
      - Measure wall-clock time for:
          (a) average proxy eval time per graph (including generation + both metrics)
          (b) average training+robustness time per trained model (per seed), from existing training logs
      - Report ratio = full_eval_time / proxy_time (should be >> 100)

Plot output (Plot 1 specification):
  Panel A: Scatter of all proxy graphs in ( \hat{TE}, \widehat{|ORC|} )
    - All graphs: light markers
    - Pareto set: highlighted
    - Selected K: large markers + labels (S1..SK)

  Panel B: Cost bars (log scale recommended)
    - Proxy eval time per graph
    - Training+robustness time per model (per seed)
    - Annotate ratio

Expected results / hypotheses:
  H1: Proxy space exhibits broad coverage (not a narrow line), and Pareto set is nontrivial.
  H2: Proxy evaluation is orders of magnitude cheaper than full evaluation.

Go/No-go checks (must run before proceeding):
  - If Pareto set size is tiny (<10 at N_proxy=500), selection may be unstable; increase N_proxy or broaden generator bounds (only within first-pass allowed bounds).
  - If cost ratio is not large, method narrative weakens; verify timing measurement correctness (exclude I/O overhead, include training to convergence).

Reuse vs updates:
  Reuse:
    - Existing WS-Flex generator implementation and metric computation.
  Update:
    - Ensure TE metric used is DEGREE ENTROPY normalized /5.0 clipped.
    - Ensure ORC uses magnitude normalized /10.0 clipped.
    - Ensure disconnected graphs rejected consistently with first-pass.
    - Implement/confirm Pareto extraction + diversity selection (if not already present).

