6) EXPERIMENT 3 (PLOT 3): PROXIES AS STRUCTURAL COORDINATES (ORGANIZE TRAINED LANDSCAPE + HIT-RATE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Motivation:
  Even if correlation is modest, proxies are valuable if they provide a coordinate system that helps find robust regions.
  NeurIPS reviewers often accept “proxies organize” more readily than “proxies perfectly predict.”

Core questions:
  Q3a: In the proxy plane ( \hat{TE}, \widehat{|ORC|} ), do trained robustness outcomes cluster into identifiable regions/bands?
  Q3b: Does proxy-based selection increase the probability of landing in the “robust” subset compared to uniform?

Inputs:
  Use the trained results from Experiment 2 (no new training required).

Procedure:
  E3.1 Proxy-plane robustness map:
    - For each trained topology (WS-Flex only: G1 and G2):
        record point ( \hat{TE}, \widehat{|ORC|} ) and its robustness metric (RD_max or AUPC).
    - Create a binned aggregation in proxy plane:
        Option A (simple): 2D grid bins; compute mean RD_max in each occupied bin.
        Option B (smoother): kNN smoothing in proxy plane (avoid if code/time constraints).

  E3.2 Robustness–accuracy tradeoff scatter:
    - For each trained run:
        x = a_0 (clean ROC-AUC)
        y = RD_max (lower better)   [or y = AUPC higher better if available]
      Mark whether run is from proxy-selected or uniform-selected topology.
    - Goal: show proxy selection concentrates in favorable region (high a_0, low RD_max).

  E3.3 Hit-rate analysis (primary statistic for “pluckability”):
    Define “robust set” threshold:
      Option A (recommended): robust = lowest 20% RD_max among WS-Flex trained runs.
      Option B: robust = RD_max < τ where τ is a fixed domain threshold (only if you have a compelling τ).
    Compute:
      hit_rate_proxy = P(robust | topology ∈ G1)
      hit_rate_uniform = P(robust | topology ∈ G2)
    Report hit-rate ratio and bootstrap CI for the difference.

Plot output (Plot 3 specification):
  Panel A: Proxy plane scatter (trained WS-Flex only)
    - x: \hat{TE}, y: \widehat{|ORC|}
    - color: RD_max (or AUPC)
    - marker: selected vs uniform
    - optional: binned heatmap underlay to show region structure

  Panel B: Accuracy–robustness scatter
    - x: clean AUC a_0
    - y: RD_max
    - marker/color: selected vs uniform
    - optional: show baseline points (dense/random-sparse/NCP) in a separate legend color; if included, clearly note they have no proxy coordinates.

Expected results / hypotheses:
  H5: Robustness is not purely random in proxy space; robust models cluster in regions (bands) in the proxy plane.
  H6: hit_rate_proxy > hit_rate_uniform (proxy improves chance of selecting robust models).

Go/No-go checks:
  - If hit-rate improvement is absent, your narrative weakens. If correlation is low but hit-rate is improved, that’s acceptable and often stronger.
  - If both are absent, the proxy story is in trouble; verify metric implementations and selection procedure.

Reuse vs updates:
  Reuse:
    - Results tables/logs from Experiment 2.
  Update:
    - Add hit-rate computation and bootstrap CI.
    - Add proxy-plane binned aggregation (minimal code).

